config BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_USB_INPUT
	bool "cadr-usb-input"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_COMMON
	select BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_TERMINAL
	help
	  A USB keyboard and mouse plugged into the board, carried to the
	  CADR's own keyboard and mouse.  With it the machine can be used
	  at the board rather than only through a viewer on another
	  machine over the network.

	  It reads /dev/input/event* and sends keysyms and mouse movement
	  to cadr-terminal over a local socket; that program writes the
	  I/O board's registers.  There is one queue behind those
	  registers and the rate at which words may be handed over is a
	  rule about the machine, so one program paces them and everything
	  else is a source --- which is how the reference emulator is
	  arranged too, with one keyboard and up to eight viewers pushing
	  into it.  docs/usb-input.md has the decision.

	  It selects cadr-terminal for that reason: without it there is
	  nothing to send to.  It maps no memory and reaches no port of
	  its own.

	  It has an init script, S88, after the terminal's S85.
